  "interpretation": [
    "Kernel accounts for about 70 percent of extra guest attempts. Both increased traffic and extra work per event contribute.",
    "Identical recorded entries in ggc_alloc_stat and recog_32 but larger self counts demonstrate extra code-path work without more entries. They do not by themselves isolate compiler code generation from changed branch paths or object sizes.",
    "Earlier mapping/request traces on the same application binaries show doubled pointer-bearing allocation sizes and 118 versus 281 mapping requests during compilation. That older trace used an earlier kernel; do not equate those phase counts with whole-run counts above.",
    "The native syscall path is capability-aware Linux integration, not an identical stock Linux ABI. Removing external-module transport does not remove allocator, lifetime and page-management responsibilities."
  ],
  "limitations": [
